+/// Transaction root for the payload in [`CACHE`].  Engine payloads carry raw
+/// transactions but not the root as a separate field, so the generic Engine API
+/// conversion normally rebuilds the whole trie.  N42's compact-block path
+/// already authenticated this root when the leader built the block; retaining
+/// it lets followers avoid repeating that serial work while the final block-hash
+/// comparison still validates the supplied root.
+static TRANSACTION_ROOT_CACHE: OnceLock<Mutex<Option<(B256, B256)>>> = OnceLock::new();
 
